        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Team Desmond Keany and Leonard Wilson Keenan are delighted to present\r\n54 Nephin Road, Dublin 7 to the market.\r\n\r\nA Rare A2‑Rated 4 Bedroom End‑of‑Terrace Home in a Premier, Mature Residential Location\r\nCorner Site • Triple‑Glazed • Wrap‑Around Garden • 153 sq.m • Off‑Street Parking\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is strongly advised.\r\n\r\nTeam Desmond Keany and Leonard Wilson Keenan are delighted to present this exceptional A2‑rated, recently constructed (Built in 2022) end‑of‑terrace family home to the Dublin 7 market — a premium and rare find, as A‑rated homes of this calibre are exceptionally scarce in such an established and mature residential neighbourhood.\r\n\r\nLocated just 400 metres from the Phoenix Park, No. 54 combines modern energy‑efficient design with generous internal space and a prime position in one of Dublin’s most desirable communities.\r\n\r\nSet on a corner site, the home enjoys a striking dual‑aspect brick elevation complemented by a freshly painted render, delivering superb natural light throughout. Extending to 153 sq.m (1,648 sq.ft) over three floors, this substantial property offers flexible accommodation ideal for families,  and those seeking a standout home beside the Phoenix Park.\r\n\r\nA bright entrance hallway leads to a large front sitting room overlooking Nephin Road. To the rear, the impressive open‑plan dine‑in kitchen and living area features a bespoke fitted kitchen, extended counter space, and utility room opening to the wrap‑around landscaped rear garden. A separate utility room and a shower room complete the ground floor.\r\n\r\nThe first floor comprises three bedrooms — two generous doubles, including a principal bedroom with walk‑in wardrobe and ensuite, and a large single bedroom ideal as a home office. A beautifully finished family bathroom, storeroom and hot press complete this level.\r\n\r\nThe second floor provides a third double bedroom with its own ensuite  and a large  attic room, offering excellent privacy and versatility for guests, older children or remote working.\r\n\r\nExternally, the home continues to impress. The front driveway is finished with quality paving, providing secure off‑street parking. The wrap‑around rear garden is fully enclosed, low‑maintenance, and enhanced with raised planters and a broad side entrance — a rare advantage in Dublin 7.\r\n\r\nAlready boasting an A2 BER, triple‑glazed windows/doors, and an air‑to‑water heat pump, No. 54 is an economical home with scope to further enhance efficiency through solar panels and EV car charging.\r\nA2‑rated homes are exceptionally rare in Dublin 7, making this property a standout premium offering.\r\n\r\nThe location offers outstanding connectivity and convenience:\r\nCabra Gate entrance to the Phoenix Park — 400m\r\nNavan Road (R147) — 130m, with direct access to the M50 (5km)\r\nN2 orbital bus stop directly outside the door (Clontarf Road–Heuston)\r\nRoutes 37, 38, 39, 70 and 122 serve the city centre, DCU, UCD and Blanchardstown.\r\nBroombridge Luas Green Line & Commuter Rail — 20‑minute walk\r\nCity centre 4–5km | Dublin Airport 12km\r\nMater Hospital and Connolly Hospital Blanchardstown are within easy reach.\r\nSchools, Aura Leisure Centre and Inspire Leisure Centre all within walking distance\r\nLocal shopping, childcare, cafés, restaurants, supermarkets and leisure facilities are all easily accessible. Phibsborough, Stoneybatter and TU Dublin’s Grangegorman campus are also close at hand.\r\n\r\nNo. 54 Nephin Road represents a rare chance to acquire a premium, energy‑efficient, beautifully finished 4‑bedroom home in one of Dublin 7’s most established and sought‑after residential locations. Early viewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
